course: dictionary
lesson: 3022
title: Dynasty: rulers passed down through a family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dynasty is a line of rulers from the same family, where power passes from parent to child over many years. The context tells you this: «China was ruled by dynasties, families passing power from parent to child.» Those words are the clue, so dynasty means a family that rules in a line.
explain: Dates in a sentence help too. «The Qing dynasty, 1644–1912» shows that a dynasty lasts a long time, from a start year to an end year. The time one family rules is also called a dynasty.
explain: Sometimes the word is used in a new way. «A football dynasty» is not about kings. Ask yourself what would fit: a team that wins for many seasons, just as a royal family stays in power for many years. That is figurative use, a meaning beyond the first one.
fact: A dynasty is a line of rulers from the same family.
fact: «Dynasty» can also mean the time when one family rules, such as «the Ming dynasty».
fact: Historians use dynasties to split long histories into periods, such as the Tudors in England.
fact: «Dynasty» can describe a family or team that stays successful for many years, as in «a football dynasty».
fact: Ming: «Most of the Great Wall you see in photos today was built or rebuilt by the Ming dynasty.»
exercise: «China was ruled by dynasties, families passing power from parent to child.» What is a dynasty? | *A line of rulers from the same family | A kind of paper made from plants | A type of castle wall | A kettle for boiling water
exercise: «a football dynasty» means what? | A football match played in a castle | A ball made from leather | A team that always loses | *A team that stays successful for many years
exercise: «The Qing dynasty, 1644–1912» tells us what about the Qing? | *It ruled for a long time, from 1644 to 1912 | It was a very small village | It ruled for only one day | It was a sport played on a hill
test: Power passes from parent to child over many years. What is this kind of rule called? | A market | *A dynasty | A republic | A democracy
test: «Most of the Great Wall you see in photos today was built or rebuilt by the Ming dynasty.» Which dynasty built most of it? | *The Ming | The Yuan | The Han | The Tang
exam: Which example means a team that stays successful for many years? | *A football dynasty | The Tudors ruled England | Dadu was a city in China | The Qing dynasty ruled China
